    {
      "before": "<p>(b) $C=F(S_{(18)})\\sim$ Beta$(18,2)$: mean $0.9$, variance $\\frac{18\\cdot2}{20^2\\cdot21}=0.00429$, standard deviation $0.065$. $C\\lt0.8$ iff at least $18$ of $19$ uniforms lie below $0.8$: $19\\cdot0.8^{18}\\cdot0.2+0.8^{19}=0.083$, about one calibration set in twelve.</p>",
      "after": "<p>(b) $C=F(S_{(18)})\\sim$ Beta$(18,2)$: mean $0.9$, variance $\\frac{18\\cdot2}{20^2\\cdot21}=3/700\\approx0.00429$, standard deviation $\\sqrt{3/700}\\approx0.065$. $C\\lt0.8$ iff at least $18$ of $19$ uniforms lie below $0.8$: $19\\cdot0.8^{18}\\cdot0.2+0.8^{19}\\approx0.083$, about one calibration set in twelve.</p>",
      "count": 1,
      "reason": "The genuine Beta18,2 density integrals derive variance3/700 and the exact strict-CDF binomial polynomial. The printed variance and probability decimals are rigorously certified nearest-place approximations and strictly unequal to the actual quantities."
    },
    {
      "before": "<p>(c) Given $C$, the test count is Bin$(2000,C)$. Total variance: $\\operatorname{Var}C+\\mathbb E[C(1-C)]/2000=0.004286+0.0857/2000=0.004329$, standard deviation $0.0658$. The calibration set dominates; the finite test set adds only 1% to the variance.</p>",
      "after": "<p>(c) Given $C$, the test count is Bin$(2000,C)$. Total variance: $\\operatorname{Var}C+\\mathbb E[C(1-C)]/2000=3/700+(3/35)/2000=303/70000\\approx0.004329$, standard deviation $\\sqrt{303/70000}\\approx0.0658$. The calibration set dominates; the finite test set adds only 1% to the variance.</p>",
      "count": 1,
      "reason": "Use the genuine exact Beta variance and expected conditional Bernoulli variance in the total-variance identity, then qualify the final finite decimal. The added variance divided by calibration variance is exactly1/100; both displayed standard deviations have true certified roundings."
    }
  ],
